**SECURED — first-secure ride on the unclaimed `e3-blackout-ridge`**: waves 12 / 360.000s / 200 gold / 88 kills / 47 calls, zero defaulted picks, zero defaulted secures, eventLogHash `fnv1a32:43f08074`. The tape put forward is `artifacts/heat11/fable/e3-blackout-ridge/attempt-1-tape.json` (scored attempt 1 of 2 allowed) — a deterministic re-run of the first honest full ride, with input log and outcome byte-identical between the two tapes. Four sim runs total: idle probe (reproduced the published null floor bit-for-bit), one controller-bug ride, the securing tune, and the scored re-run. Stopped on first secured outcome per the rules. worldModel: `sim-import`.

What decided it — three reads of the era's power graph, all in the negative:

1. **No turrets on this board.** The buildables list sells only beacons/palisades/sluices/stockpiles/assay_office/capacitor_bank, so the guns are the hero's auto-blast plus three fort sentry beacons priced 55/75/95 (the curve continues past the three pre-placed trunk frames).
2. **REPAIR_UNDER is an exile trap here**: it selects the *first-registered* wrecked-or-damaged work — the pre-placed trunk relay frames 60wu southwest, chewed by saboteurs from wave 1 and matching at any pct once wrecked. One repair order would have marched the Prospector across the map forever. I never sent it; 10g palisades were the repair substitute.
3. **The doomed trunk is an aggro sink**: the wrecker population pinned at the 60-enemy cap grinding the far SW yard, and waves 8–12 never touched the fort at all. The capacitor/lamp storage story is unreachable-not-required — both storage nodes boot offline and the secure latch has no connect clause.

Margin was wide: hero never below 92/100 (117/125 after plating), all fort works standing at the bank. The report with the four operator-copied sections, the outcome JSON, controller, tapes, and logs are all in the workspace. One honesty note recorded in the report: a sibling rig's artifacts existed in this clone and I did not open them — every fact came from the county's published assets, the sim source, and my own rides.
